# Openstage

> Openstage turns your GitHub commits, milestones, and notes into one automatically-updated build-in-public timeline. Builders claim a public profile at openstage.dev/their-username and share it with a single link.

Openstage is a build-in-public profile for developers and indie hackers. It reads your public GitHub commit activity and lets you add milestones and notes by hand, producing one chronological timeline. It is free to start. Openstage Pro is $7/month or $49 one-time and adds profile analytics, private entries, pinned entries, and a Pro badge. Openstage never posts on a user's behalf, and there are no likes or comments — it is a timeline, not a social network.

