## How it works
- Sign in with GitHub and claim a username.
- Public commits sync automatically into a chronological timeline, grouped by repository.
- Add milestones (launches, wins) and notes (decisions, lessons) by hand for context.
- Turn the last 7, 30 or 90 days of commits into a post: Openstage lists them, the builder ticks the lines worth sharing, edits the text freely, and posts it themselves on X or Bluesky. Openstage never writes, ranks or posts on their behalf.
- Share one link at openstage.dev/your-username, complete with a social preview card, an embeddable badge and an RSS feed. Visitors can subscribe by email; the builder owns that list.

